<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pierre Laval</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1883–1945</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pierre Laval was a French politician who served as prime minister in the 1930s and became the leading figure of collaboration in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vichy">Vichy</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. As head of government from 1942 to 1944 he worked closely with Nazi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, sending French workers to the Reich and assisting the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deportation">deportation</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a>. After the Liberation he was tried for treason and executed in October 1945.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pierre-laval.jpg" alt="Pierre Laval" width="320" height="415" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Agence de presse Meurisse · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pierre_Laval_a_Meurisse_1931.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
